#
# Counter-example for gmeow:TopologyClaimStatusConstraint (gmeow:TopologyClaimMissingStatus,
# Req 6): a gmeow:TopologyClaim that carries its inherited gmeow:observationMethod (so the
# gmeow:StandpointClaim exactly-one observation-method obligation is satisfied and NOT the
# violation under test) and its result, but carries NO gmeow:vantage attribution. A computed
# feature must land as a vantage-attributed, defeasible claim, so the ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint
# MUST reject it with shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent, and nothing else — the anonymous,
# unattributed claim is the sole violation.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/semantic-topology/tests/> .

ex:claimBad a gmeow:TopologyClaim ;
    gmeow:observationMethod gmeow:methodComputationalModel ;   # StandpointClaim obligation satisfied
    gmeow:claimResult ex:result .                              # <-- but NO gmeow:vantage

ex:result a gmeow:TopologyResult .
